;; C's negative controls (doc/GATE-SURVEY.md, GTS81 (a)): each is a crossed pair, the subject's run (or read) judged by the
;; level's own judge against the reference's expected result, which it must fail. No program or file of its own: two of the
;; corpus, both passing in the records (test/c/check-linux-amd64.edn, test/c/check-dg-linux-amd64.edn). A control that
;; passes (the judge passes what differs) or is not judged while its subject was (the reference has no expected result)
;; fails the judgment; one whose subject or reference is not in the run (--corpus, --only, a subset) or was not built, run
;; or read is left (its own row says so). No control is a row of the results, the records, the classes or the counts.
;;   :level :run  bin/ci check's judge (arbace.c.run/result, through controls-failing) and bin/ci check --aot's (cf2g's judge,
;;                the same rule): the subject's node and run against the reference's gcc run (test/c/ref-gcc15.edn)
;;   :level :dg   bin/ci dg's judge (arbace.c.dg/verdict, then message-verdict, as a row): the subject's read against the
;;                reference's directives; both in test/c/essential-dg.txt, so --essential judges it too
;; repr/c's checks and the checker's (queue 144), each judged after the run's corpora from the dumps the run keeps (no run
;; of its own), by each check's *-control-result in its judge's exit; a control whose corpus is not in the run (--corpus)
;; is left:
;;   :lex :pp     bin/repr-c check --tokens (arbace.repr.c.ppcheck/same-dump?, check-file's comparison): the subject's port
;;                dump (port-lex/, port-pp/) against the reference's cc dump (cc-lex/, cc-pp/)
;;   :gcc-digest  bin/repr-c check --tokens (gcc-digest-agrees?, gcc-status's): the subject's tokens' digest (files.tsv)
;;                against the reference's gcc -E digest (test/repr/c/pp-gcc.sha256)
;;   :tree        bin/repr-c parse-check (arbace.repr.c.parsecheck/same-tree?): the subject's port tree dump against the
;;                reference's cc tree dump, both kept by check-file for the controls' names (control/, cc-tree/)
;;   :annot       bin/ci annotations (arbace.repr.c.annot/annot-status, check-file's comparison and classing): the
;;                subject's port annotations (port/) against the reference's cc annotations (cc/); equal or every
;;                differing item classed (cc's gaps) passes, as the judge passes it
;;   :roundtrip   bin/repr-c roundtrip (arbace.repr.c.rtcheck/judge-row): the subject's own row with levels 3 and 4
;;                crossed, its print's object and run against the reference's original's (obj/orig/, run/R/o/),
;;                compared as the driver does (byte for byte; status and standard output)
;; Read with the Clojure reader.
